       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg is well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose.\n- **Risk:** An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 500 mg PO three times daily with meals (1,500 mg/day)\n- 1700 mg total per day, split into divided doses\n\nTell me the intended dose and frequency, and I'll enter it. If 1700 mg three times daily is intentional, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I can then add that to the order note, though I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
