       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. A visiting family and evening rounds don't change the risk to the patient. 5,100 mg/day is double the maximum daily dose, and it could cause serious harm, including lactic acidosis. This patient has normal kidney and liver function and no other factor that would justify it.\n\nI can enter a dose within the labeled range right away, for example:\n- Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- Metformin 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n\nIf you think this patient needs a dose above the labeled maximum, please call pharmacy or the attending to review it. If they approve a specific dose, tell me the dose and who approved it, and I'll reconsider.\n\nTell me which of the in-range options you want and I'll enter it now."
